Calendar-managed meetings now require the calendar integration's OAuth client to be configured: set `galley.config.settings.meetings.calendarOAuthClients` to the OAuth client id(s) of the calendar integration. Until it is set, no caller can create or mutate externally-managed meetings. OAuth access tokens issued before this release carry no client id and must be refreshed. Upgrade nginz before setting `calendarOAuthClients`: galley trusts the `Z-OAuth-Client` header, which only the new nginz sets from the verified token and strips from client requests; an ingress path to galley that does not strip it would let any OAuth app claim to be the calendar integration.
